---
import PublicLayout from "../layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
---

<PublicLayout
  currentPath="/features"
  description="See how Kinship will keep relationship context, thoughtful follow-through, and personal history together."
  pageId="public.features"
  title="Features — Kinship"
>
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="features-intro" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Designed around people</p>
        <h1 id="features-heading">Thoughtful tools for showing up.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="availability-note">
        <strong>Available as Kinship grows</strong>
        These are the concrete capabilities we are building toward. The public
        preview is live today; the private workspace is still in active
        development.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="feature-list" aria-label="Product capabilities">
      <article>
        <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">01 · CONTEXT</span>
        <h2>One home for each person</h2>
        <p>
          Bring contact details, important dates, relationships, notes, and
          shared history into one person-centered workspace.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">02 · FOLLOW-THROUGH</span>
        <h2>Gentle, timely prompts</h2>
        <p>
          Keep promises visible with reminders, tasks, and stay-in-touch rhythms
          that support care without turning people into a pipeline.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">03 · HISTORY</span>
        <h2>Meaningful moments in context</h2>
        <p>
          See conversations, activities, notes, and life events in the place
          where they make sense: alongside the person they concern.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="feature-number" aria-hidden="true">04 · CONTROL</span>
        <h2>Your private record, portable</h2>
        <p>
          Kinship is designed for workspace isolation and clear data ownership,
          with import and export paths planned as first-class capabilities.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</PublicLayout>
